WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.518 --> 00:00:01.740
(gentle music)

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:04.230
- [Narrator] This satellite
image shows destroyed vehicles

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.470
scattered around the frontline
village of Novodonetske

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:08.970
in Eastern Ukraine,

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.670
which had a population
of several hundred people

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:12.960
before the war.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.850
Russian state media shared a video

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:18.060
suggesting that a column of
Ukrainian armored vehicles

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.460
and Western tanks was destroyed

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.890
after running over a minefield.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.840
The footage was released around the time

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.840
Ukraine's counteroffensive
started in early June 2023.

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:30.682
(explosion booming)

00:00:30.682 --> 00:00:33.570
Kyiv says, "The sheer
number of Russian landmines

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.360
on the battlefield is
hampering its militaries push

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.360
to retake territory."
(missiles booming)

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.780
Here's how Russia created
one of the biggest minefields

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:43.743
in the world.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.770
Ukraine's counteroffensive
focused on the Zaporizhzhia

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:51.480
and Donetsk regions.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.320
Russian-held Novodonetske
is right in this area.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.380
But Kyiv's forces quickly
ran into obstacles.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:02.250
Russia spent months preparing
the 900 mile long frontline

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:05.040
with anti-tank ditches, concrete blocks,

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.980
trenches, and landmines.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:11.610
It's estimated that
approximately 60,000 square miles

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.730
of land, more than 1/4 of the country,

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:19.374
may now be littered with anti
personnel and anti-tank mines.

00:01:19.374 --> 00:01:23.291
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:25.465 --> 00:01:26.430
(explosion booming)

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:29.130
- [Narrator] Ukraine's Security
Council Secretary in August

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:32.640
estimated that Ukrainian
forces were encountering fields

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.613
with up to five mines per 10 square feet.

00:01:36.568 --> 00:01:38.220
(missiles booming)

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:41.460
Videos shared online by
Russian state media journalists

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:45.210
and pro-war bloggers show
Russia's brand new remote

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:49.473
mine laying system known as
Zemledeliye or Agriculture.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:54.870
First unveiled in 2020, the
system made its combat debut

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:57.540
in Ukraine in the early months of the war.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:01.080
According to defense
intelligence firm, Janes.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.380
Russian state media say the
system can set a whole minefield

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.330
three to nine miles away

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:10.293
using a single salvo of
50 mine loaded rockets.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.687
Janes expert, the
journal spoke with, says,

00:02:13.687 --> 00:02:17.100
"Zemledeliye is one of a
number of systems Russia uses

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.888
to literally sow the
frontline with mines."

00:02:20.888 --> 00:02:22.370
(tank engine revving)

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:26.287
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:36.210
- [Narrator] The minefield
slowed down Ukrainian forces

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.880
and channeled advancing
infantry into positions

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.680
where they would be an easy targets

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.700
for Russian helicopters,
artillery, and drones.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:48.420
After losing a number of Western
tanks and armored vehicles,

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:51.090
the Ukrainian military switch tactics.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:53.490
Now infantry are leading the advances

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.999
through the minefields on foot.

00:02:55.999 --> 00:02:59.916
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:00.982 --> 00:03:01.815
(missiles booming)

00:03:01.815 --> 00:03:03.660
- [Narrator] Military
analysts also say Ukraine

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.700
has been firing more artillery,

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.560
as well as using Western missiles

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:10.110
such as British Storm Shadows to target

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:12.303
Russian supply lines from afar.

00:03:13.383 --> 00:03:15.120
(explosion booming)

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.090
The military experts with
Janes says for Ukraine

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:21.060
time is running out
before the weather changes

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.370
and large scale movements
become constrained

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.663
by the muddy ground.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.040
In mid-August, Ukraine's
military made some advances,

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.883
retaking a village some six
miles away from Novodonetske.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.060
This shows that while
Russian defense lines

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:40.149
remain a major obstacle,
they can be penetrated.

00:03:40.149 --> 00:03:42.816
(gentle music)

